| data-row-id="sigil-of-the-dead" style="text-align:center;" | [[File:Sigil of the Dead.png|80px]]<br/> Sigil of the Dead || Your '''Call''' becomes '''Hades' Aid''' , which briefly makes you '''Invisible'''; your '''God Gauge''' starts {{Green|10/20/30%}} full. <br> <br> Stealth Damage Bonus: <br> '''+50/{{Rare|75}}/{{Epic|100}}%'''  || ''From [[Hades]]; you share an Intractable Bond. <br> <br> The feared and distant Underworld King knows that his hardest work is still ahead of him.'' ||
*Hades' Aid counts as a boon and can be upgraded, but maxes out at Epic rarity.
*Hades' Aid cannot gain levels from Poms, however. 
*The Sigil of the Dead cannot be equipped if another god's Aid has been chosen.
*While Invisible, [[Zagreus]] cannot be targeted, moves +50% faster, and deals bonus damage for 2 seconds (or until he strikes).
**At Max Gauge, Zagreus turns '''Unseen''' instead of Invisible, increasing bonus damage to 5 seconds and not expiring when Zagreus strikes.
*Activating the Call removes all of the effects:
**[[Status_effects#Styx_Poison|Styx Poison]]
**[[Status_effects#Petrified|Gorgon Petrified]]
**Hit Stun due to self damage by [[Adamant_Rail#Upgrades|Hazard Bomb]]
**[[Status_effects#Charmed|Charmed]]
**[[Status_effects#Status_Curses|Chill]]
** [[Wringer|Wringer's]] grasp
* It also removes Hades' Skull Casts from the ground, but not the Boiling Blood debuff.
*The Sigil is one of two Keepsakes that can only be acquired after finishing the main story, the other being the [[Pom Blossom]].
